From 646c886ac68407f34f05985102d4b68c3b53678a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: palazik <gochmyradov0@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:47:44 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] dodge: use the iOS user address space, not the macOS one

First real fallout from the 4K switch, caught by a static assertion
rather than at runtime:

  pmap.c:10987: (_COMM_PAGE64_BASE_ADDRESS & ~ARM_TT_L1_OFFMASK)
                >= MACH_VM_MAX_ADDRESS

The commpage sits at 64GB-16K, so with 4K pages it rounds down to 63GB
and must still be above the top of the user address space. It is not,
because building as a MacOSX platform target selects a 127TB user VA -
which this configuration cannot represent anyway: that needs 47 bits
(T0SZ 17), and 4K here gives T0SZ 25, a 39-bit 512GB space.

We build as MacOSX only to get the right SDK; the target is a phone. So
take the value the non-MacOSX branch already has, 63GB, which fits the
39-bit space and satisfies the assertion. The iOS userland we intend to
run expects that layout regardless.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 osfmk/mach/arm/vm_param.h | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/osfmk/mach/arm/vm_param.h b/osfmk/mach/arm/vm_param.h
index c013288..6b866c9 100644
--- a/osfmk/mach/arm/vm_param.h
+++ b/osfmk/mach/arm/vm_param.h
@@ -133,7 +133,19 @@ extern int PAGE_SHIFT_CONST;
 
 /* system-wide values */
 #define MACH_VM_MIN_ADDRESS_RAW 0x0ULL
-#if defined(XNU_PLATFORM_MacOSX) || defined(XNU_PLATFORM_DriverKit)
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_DODGE)
+/*
+ * dodge is a phone, and builds with 4K pages because its Oryon cores do not
+ * implement the 16K granule. It is only built as a MacOSX platform target to
+ * get the right SDK, so take the iOS user address space rather than the macOS
+ * one, which this configuration cannot represent: the macOS 127TB value needs
+ * a 47-bit user VA (T0SZ 17), while 4K here gives T0SZ 25, a 39-bit 512GB
+ * space. It also breaks the commpage invariant that pmap.c asserts for 4K -
+ * _COMM_PAGE64_BASE_ADDRESS sits at 64GB, so it cannot nest above a 127TB
+ * user VA, and the build fails there rather than silently later.
+ */
+#define MACH_VM_MAX_ADDRESS_RAW 0x0000000FC0000000ULL
+#elif defined(XNU_PLATFORM_MacOSX) || defined(XNU_PLATFORM_DriverKit)
 #define MACH_VM_MAX_ADDRESS_RAW 0x00007FFFFE000000ULL
 #else
 #define MACH_VM_MAX_ADDRESS_RAW 0x0000000FC0000000ULL
